<Root>
  <DefaultMacro>
    <Major>Weapons (Recoil Control)</Major>
    <Description>5-Point Diagonal Jitter
Driver: Must be ENABLED in the settings ("Use driver for mouse control in macros").
Resolution: 1920x1080.
DPI: 800 DPI.
Mode: Loop while pressed.
3px horizontal, 3px down dip between every step.

It works great for all weapons, just know this isnt "Zero" recoil rather heavily reduces it espically for lower recoil weapons. R99 and Car need a touch of pulling down to remove all recoil. happy shooting</Description>
    <Comment>1. Set execution mode to "Loop while pressed".
2. Driver must be ENABLED.
3. 800 DPI, 1920x1080.</Comment>
    <GUIOption>
      <RepeatType>1</RepeatType>
    </GUIOption>
    <KeyUp>
      <Syntax></Syntax>
    </KeyUp>
    <KeyDown>
      <Syntax>LeftDown 1
MoveR 3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR -3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR -3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR -3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR -3 0
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 3
Delay 1 ms
MoveR 0 -3
Delay 1 ms
Goto 2</Syntax>
    </KeyDown>
    <Software>Apex Legends</Software>
  </DefaultMacro>
</Root>